    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n    <span class=\"time\">55 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Deep dive</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\">Trees</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Trees: LCA, views, distance-K and serialization</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Lowest common ancestor in a binary tree, in a BST and with parent pointers; right, left, top, vertical and boundary views; all nodes at distance K; serialize and deserialize; and rebuilding a tree from two traversals. These questions come up again and again at Meta, Amazon, Microsoft, LinkedIn and Flipkart. This page builds each one from a picture to a template in Go, C++, Java and Python.</p>\n"
